{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>And the Levite shall come.</b> And he shall take the first tithe." "<b>And the stranger and the orphan.</b> And they shall take the second tithe, which is the poor man's tithe of this year — and you do not eat it in Jerusalem, in the manner that you needed to eat the second tithe of the two years [preceding]." "<b>And they shall eat and be satisfied.</b> Give them enough for their satisfaction — from here the Sages said: one may not give the poor less at the threshing floor, etc. (Sifrei 110). And you go up to Jerusalem with the tithe of the first and second years that you delayed, and make the declaration: ״בִּעַרְתִּי הַקֹּדֶשׁ מִן הַבַּיִת״ — as is spelled out in כִּי תְכַלֶּה לַעְשֵׂר (Deuteronomy 26)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:47:08.480206002Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}